The online softmax. The lab target smx asked whether a single-pass softmax pays on the v79, against
the three passes of 0060: the maximum, then the exponential with its sum into a pad, then the
normalization of the pad. The online form merges the first two passes: it keeps a running maximum
and multiplies the running sum by exp(m_old - m_new) when the maximum moves. The three-pass form
evaluates the exponential one time for each element and keeps the result. The online form cannot,
because the final maximum is not known until the row ends. Thus its second pass must evaluate the
exponential again or multiply each stored block by exp(m_block - M), and the two cost one
exponential for each vector. The online form thus replaces a cheap pass of loads and maximums with
an expensive pass. The landed kernel keeps the three passes. The target needed the grouped
exponential of 0060, thus it could not run against the tree, and it left the lab with 0060.
